# Docker rebuilds everything fresh inside its own container, so none of
# this needs to be sent as build context. Without this file, `docker
# compose build web` was sending the entire proxynexus-package/ directory
# (23GB+) as context on every build -- confirmed the actual breakdown:
# proxynexus-rs/target/ (11GB Rust build cache), leftover .pnx test
# artifacts (5.6GB), and data/collections/ (6.7GB, which the `web` build
# doesn't even use -- minio-init mounts it directly as a volume instead,
# see docker-compose.yml). This is what caused a real "no space left on
# device" build failure.
proxynexus-rs/target/
proxynexus-rs/*.pnx
proxynexus-rs/*.pdf
proxynexus-rs/*_mpc.zip
proxynexus-rs/.git/
data/collections/
.git/
